lia.rs is licensed under MIT. Its inference implementation is written in Rust.

src/codebooks.rs contains GGML IQ quantization codebook constants from llama.cpp:
https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
Reference revision: 1268edac579110aeb1407f7928f53193ed4e28d4
The chunked recurrent algorithm and BF16 residual matrix-product approach
were also informed by ggml-cuda/gated-delta-net-mma.cu at that revision.
The corresponding Rust operators are implemented independently.
The vision layout and image resampling behavior were informed by
tools/mtmd/models/qwen3vl.cpp and tools/mtmd/mtmd-image.cpp at that revision.
The Rust preprocessing and vision operators are implemented independently.
The grouped-to-interleaved GDN value-head layout was checked against
conversion/qwen.py at the same revision; the Rust loader is independent.
The reference sampling seed streams and stochastic draft rejection behavior
were informed by common/sampling.cpp and common/speculative.cpp at that
revision; the Rust sampler and verification implementation are independent.

